# Cursor Rules for idp

## Memory (shared across all agents)

This repo has persistent memory via MCP. Use it to remember decisions, learn context, and avoid re-asking.

### MCP Server (if your client supports MCP)
```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "memory": {
      "command": "/Users/roseonyema/Documents/code/estate-core/memory/mcp_server.py"
    }
  }
}
```

Tools available:
- `memory_write` — store facts, decisions, observations
- `memory_recall` — query what you've learned
- `memory_ambient` — get context-aware suggestions

### REST API (fallback for any agent)
```bash
# Start the server (needs Neo4j running)
uvicorn estate-core.memory.a2m_server:app --port 8787

# Write memory
curl -X POST http://localhost:8787/memory \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"content": "User prefers X over Y", "source": "cursor-agent"}'

# Recall
curl -X POST http://localhost:8787/recall \
  -d '{"query": "user preferences"}'
```

## Knowledge Graph

Run `growmos context` at session start to load the repo's knowledge graph.
Run `growmos query "your question"` before asking cross-cutting questions.
Run `growmos remember` / `growmos link` when you learn something durable.

## Estate Scripts

Guard scripts and hooks live in `/Users/roseonyema/Documents/code/estate-core/scripts/`.
These are model-agnostic Python scripts for:
- Token auditing
- Secret scrubbing
- Rule enforcement
- Session recording

## Agent Roles

Role definitions in `/Users/roseonyema/Documents/code/estate-core/agents/*.md`.
Each defines tools, model, and behavior for a specific job (PM, QA, builder, etc.).
